From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.gaming.input: IInspectable stubs, controller and provider properties, custom factory registration

The FIXME stubs of the DLL, done as Windows behaves:

- every GetIids lists the interfaces its object answers (factories,
  effects, motor, controllers, vectors, iterators, async operations);
  GetTrustLevel is BaseTrust; the factories' GetRuntimeClassName names
  their class; the vector, view and iterator class names carry the
  element type (IVectorView`1<Windows.Gaming.Input.Gamepad>); an unknown
  IID is E_NOINTERFACE without a FIXME.
- IGameControllerProvider: IsConnected, HardwareVersionInfo (the HID
  version number as major.minor), FirmwareVersionInfo (0.0.0.0).
- IGameController: the headset and user-changed events accept a handler
  and a token, Headset and User are empty, IsWireless is FALSE;
  TryGetBatteryReport succeeds with no report.
- IRawGameController: GetButtonLabel, GetSwitchKind (bounds-checked),
  NonRoamableId ({wgi/nrid/<hash of the device path>}), DisplayName (the
  HID game controller description, as dinput's tests expect).
- IGamepad2::GetButtonLabel: the Xbox label of each button.
- IRacingWheel: HasClutch, HasHandbrake, HasPatternShifter,
  MaxPatternShifterGear, MaxWheelAngle, GetButtonLabel, GetCurrentReading.
- RegisterCustomFactoryForHardwareId really registers: a device with that
  vendor and product id is also given to the factory, which is told it was
  added. (The GIP and Xusb variants validate and accept; Wine's bus has no
  such devices.) ActivateInstance of statics-only classes stays E_NOTIMPL.
- IWineGameControllerProvider gains DevicePath.

---
